# WHERE PLAY STUTTERS, measured on the real keys (perf/stutters). Three windows,
# each judged by the --stats block on exactly its own frames
# (src/systems/tour/stats_perf.gd), with every slow frame named by what it spent:
#   first-shoulder  a fresh game's FIRST press of the shoulder key, every frame
#                   printed raw: a first-use stall shows as a run of long frames
#   shoulder        walking and turning over the shoulder
#   top             walking a square looking down
#   tools/tour.sh tours/stutters.tour --stats --seed=7 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
#   tools/tour.sh tours/stutters.tour --stats --seed=4 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
# It proves nothing on its own: read the numbers, and the load beside them.
wait 5
perf stats begin
wait 1.5
hold shoulder
wait 3
perf stats end first-shoulder raw
perf stats begin
walk 0,-1 2
mouse 600,0 1.5
walk 0,-1 2
mouse -900,0 2
walk 0,-1 2 run
mouse 600,0 1.5
walk 0,-1 2
perf stats end shoulder
release shoulder
await top_view 3
wait 1.5
perf stats begin
walk 1,0 3
walk 0,1 3
walk -1,0 3
walk 0,-1 3
perf stats end top
